{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/11/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5ad8a7c0\" lines=\"10-24\">\n<description>\nConnect the innermost mirrored marker pair(s) by filling their horizontal span.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\n- Each foreground row contains exactly two foreground pixels mirrored across the vertical center.\n\nRule\n- Find the foreground row pair(s) with the smallest horizontal gap between the two markers.\n- Fill every pixel between those two markers in each selected row with the foreground color.\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- Wider marker pairs are context; the closest marker pair(s) show the unresolved horizontal segment.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"342dd610\" lines=\"18-36\">\n<description>\nMove every foreground pixel by the fixed offset indicated by its color.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a unique dominant background color.\n- The foreground is a sparse set of colored pixels.\n- Each foreground color is one of the trained motion colors: orange, red,\n  maroon, or blue.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the canvas to the background color.\n- Translate orange pixels up 2 cells, red pixels left 2 cells, maroon\n  pixels down 2 cells, and blue pixels right 1 cell.\n- Preserve each moved pixel's original color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe foreground color is the motion instruction; position only determines\nwhere that color-specific displacement lands.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"668eec9a\" lines=\"29-47\">\n<description>\nSummarize the foreground line objects as ordered horizontal color stripes.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background fills a rectangular grid.\n- Each non-background color forms one contiguous one-cell-thick line segment.\n- The line segments have distinct topmost rows, and there are at most five of\n  them.\n\nRule:\n- Sort the foreground colors by the topmost row occupied by their line\n  segment.\n- Create a 5x3 output filled with the background color.\n- Place one solid 1x3 row for each foreground color, preserving that\n  top-to-bottom order and padding any unused rows above with background.\n\nKey insight: The exact line length and slope do not matter; only the\nvertical order of the colored line segments is encoded in the output stack.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"4df5b0ae\" lines=\"27-41\">\n<description>\nPack the colored sprites along the bottom edge from smallest to largest.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background color and several monochrome 4-connected\nforeground sprites; a full-grid one-cell frame may surround the scene.\n\nRule\nRemove any full-grid rectangular frame, sort the remaining sprites by pixel\narea from smallest to largest, and paste their bounding-box sprites left to\nright with each sprite bottom-aligned.\n\nKey insight\nThe original locations do not determine the final slots; each sprite's area\ngives the packing order, while its shape and color are preserved.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bd283c4a\" lines=\"7-23\">\n<description>\nPack all pixels into color-frequency runs along bottom-up columns.\n\nInput structure\nThe input is a rectangular grid whose colors are all foreground material;\nonly the number of pixels of each color matters. In the observed task\ninstances, every present color has a distinct pixel count.\n\nRule\nCount the pixels of each color and order the colors from most frequent to\nleast frequent. Rewrite a same-size grid by placing each color's full count\nas one contiguous run while scanning columns from left to right and, within\neach column, from bottom to top.\n\nKey insight\nThe output preserves the multiset of colors but discards all original\npositions, turning the grid into a frequency-sorted column packing.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"edb79dae\" lines=\"39-53\">\n<description>\nStamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background, a rectangular single-color frame, colored placeholder cells inside the frame.\n- Outside the frame: sprite shapes (one per placeholder color) and a small legend mapping each placeholder color to an output color.\n\nRule:\n- Find the frame and its interior placeholders.\n- For each placeholder color, locate the matching-color sprite outside the frame.\n- Stamp each sprite at the placeholder's position inside the frame.\n- Recolor every stamped sprite to the output color defined by the legend.\n\nKey insight: The legend pairs (overlapping two-color glyphs outside the frame) dictate the final recoloring — placeholder color selects the shape, legend maps it to the output color.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b2bc3ffd\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\nMove every object above the solid bottom stripe upward by its own pixel count.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background, exactly one full-width non-background row\nthat acts as a fixed stripe, and one or more 4-connected monochrome objects\nabove that stripe.\n\nRule\nClear each object from its original cells, then translate it straight upward\nby the number of pixels in that object, preserving its shape and color. Leave\nthe full-width stripe unchanged.\n\nKey insight\nEach object's area is also its vertical displacement; the full-width row is a\nfixed baseline, not a moving object.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"31f7f899\" lines=\"7-21\">\n<description>\nSort vertical bars by height and redistribute them across fixed colored slots.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; a horizontal base line of a single color spans the full grid width.\n- Several monochrome vertical bars of distinct colors rise upward from the base line.\n\nRule:\n- Rank bar shapes by height (shortest to tallest).\n- Rank original x-positions (slots) left to right.\n- Place the i-th shortest shape into the i-th leftmost slot, recoloring it to that slot's original color.\n- The base line is preserved unchanged.\n\nKey insight: Each slot keeps its x-position and color identity; only the bar silhouettes are redistributed among slots by height order.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b5bb5719\" lines=\"17-32\">\n<description>\nFill the background under a top-row red/grey span with a shrinking diagonal pattern that alternates red and grey.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has an orange background.\n- All foreground pixels are red or grey and lie on the top row.\n- The first and last top-row foreground pixels define an odd-width span.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the input grid.\n- For row r below the top, fill columns span_left + r through span_right - r.\n- Each filled cell takes the top-row color r columns up-left, flipped red<->grey once per row step.\n\nKey insight:\n- The output is the top-row span propagated down-right along diagonals, while the allowable region shrinks inward from both ends each row.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"34cfa167\" lines=\"94-117\">\n<description>\nComplete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n  larger rectangle.\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\n  in the first below-control color.\n\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"53fb4810\" lines=\"105-119\">\n<description>\nExtend marker tiles outward from '+' shapes by repeating them to the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- A dominant non-bg color forms several '+'-shaped objects.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
